WEBVTT

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:04.040
When troubleshooting a knitting machine,

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:08.140
the first question to ask is,
how is your sponge bar?

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:13.180
A flat sponge bar can be the culprit
that causes a myriad of problems.

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:15.920
It doesn't matter how old your machine is

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:20.320
or how much it's been used,
the sponge material deteriorates and it

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:24.460
can no longer do the job
of holding the needles in place.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:30.060
On an LK150, it's often hard
to determine if the sponge is flat.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.580
My machine was close to 10 years old,

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:36.100
and I was really surprised
at the condition of the sponge.

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:42.020
The needles didn't seem to be loose,
but the machine just wasn't knitting well.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:48.260
Lesson learned: change your sponge
bar before you start to struggle.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:51.380
Start by removing the carriage
and the tension mast.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:55.100
Remove the clamps so you
can turn the bed over.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:57.860
And remove each of your needles.

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:02.820
Close the latch and pick up
the by the needle butt and pull it back.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.980
It should slip out pretty easily.

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:08.040
For more details about removing

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:13.060
and replacing needles,
see the video at

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.680
knititnow.Com/lk150needle.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.280
Once all the needles are out of the needle

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:21.490
bed, you may want
to take time to clean it.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:24.080
It's just plastic, so don't use any harsh

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:27.660
chemicals or cleaners
that might leave a residue.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:29.600
Just a clean paint brush
may be all you need.

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:36.100
Turn the carriage over
and remove the old sponge.

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:41.240
Position the new sponge
with the ribbon facing up.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.960
The needles will ride on this ribbon.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:55.460
We'll replace the needles
by threading them over the sponge.

00:01:55.490 --> 00:02:00.040
From the top of the bed, close
the needle latch and push the hook down.

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:05.570
use your fingers of your opposite
hand to guide the hook down.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:11.080
Then push the back of the needle
down to thread it over the sponge.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:15.760
Use your finger underneath
to guide it back into the slot.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:20.300
Do this for all 150 needles.

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:24.060
Take it slow and don't be
afraid of bending the needles.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.080
Use enough pressure to guide the needle

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:32.800
down and over the sponge and then back up
in the track towards the front of the bed.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:36.500
Replace each of the needles.

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:43.120
The LK150 originally had gray and pink
rollers every 10 needles to help you keep

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:48.440
track and position your knitting without
having to count needles every time.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.140
Once you get a new sponge bar in place,

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:54.520
you'll be amazed at how
well your machine knits.

